00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:09.850
Oh, I have my places I like to stop and snack at.

547
00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:11.970
What are they?

548
00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.030
Where will I be snacking?

549
00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:17.930
I love a good, like, just greasy burger joint.

550
00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:18.870
For sure.

551
00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:19.290
Right?

552
00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:19.730
Mm-hmm.

553
00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:23.690
Also, I love the Frito chili chips, you know?

554
00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:25.550
Oh, really?

555
00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:27.290
You're going to eat Frito chili chips around me?

556
00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:27.830
I know.

557
00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.190
Everyone says they stink up the room.

558
00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:29.990
It's so stinky, lady.

559
00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:30.370
I know.

560
00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:31.050
I love them.

561
00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:31.750
Okay.

562
00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.870
They're one of my go-to road trip snacks.

563
00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.010
Okay.

564
00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:35.630
Okay.

565
00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:36.690
All right.

566
00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:40.670
We're going to go to break now and I'm going to just try to convince Angela to eat regular Fritos.

567
00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:42.250
I love a regular Frito.

568
00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:43.890
Oh, especially with some queso.

569
00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:46.370
Oh, you know what I love a regular Frito with?

570
00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:46.690
What?

571
00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:47.910
A Frito chili pie.

572
00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:49.910
I'm so hungry now.

573
00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:50.070
Like, in the bag.

574
00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:50.750
I know.

575
00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:51.350
Give it to me.

576
00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:51.650
All right.

577
00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:52.430
We'll be back in a second.

578
00:19:52.870 --> 00:20:04.340
We are back.

579
00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.640
We're in this episode now.

580
00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:07.100
Michael, you guys.

581
00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:08.580
Oh, my gosh.

582
00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:12.360
A phone guy came in to fix his phone and showed him the PA system.

583
00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:15.320
You can't show Michael Scott the office PA system.

584
00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:17.280
You definitely cannot.

585
00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.300
He is really goofing about now.

586
00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:19.700
Yeah.

587
00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:27.180
He pretends to be a plane captain, a ghoSt. He forgets the intercom is on while he's talking to his doctor about his mole.

588
00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:31.260
He calls Toby into the principal's office for wetting his bed.

589
00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:34.780
I think we should hear it.

590
00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:35.860
Can you play the clip?

591
00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:36.280
Yeah.

592
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.040
My personal favorite part of that is the coughing.

593
00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:31.920
Yes.

594
00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:33.980
I loved listening to him cough.

595
00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:38.620
It reminded me of the tiramisu coughing fit that he had on the phone with David Wallace.

596
00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:43.640
Steve Krill is a master at fake laughing and fake coughing.

597
00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:44.060
Yeah.

598
00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:45.640
You believe it.

599
00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:48.120
We had a fan question from Virginia S.

600
00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:53.320
When Michael is on the PA system, were any of his announcements improvised or were they all in the script?

601
00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:58.360
For example, the announcement that Toby has wet his bed is hilarious.

602
00:21:59.000 --> 00:21:59.740
All right.

603
00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:01.240
They had several alts.

604
00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:05.960
And the one that was actually in the script for Toby read like this.

605
00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:11.420
Toby Flindersen to the principal's office, you are in trouble for sucking.

606
00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:13.160
That's pretty good.

607
00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:14.440
That's what was in the script.

608
00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:25.420
Well, I read the script while I watched this portion, and I would say that a lot of it was scripted, but Steve definitely did do improvisations off of what was written.

609
00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:28.420
And I'm sure Mindy was pitching things to him, too, on the day.

610
00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:28.960
Yes.

611
00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:36.120
But I noticed that the line about Ghost of Christmas Past, that was scripted, but the coughing bit was not in the script.

612
00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:42.360
Really quickly, I feel like we need to point out something at 27 seconds.

613
00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:43.320
What's that?

614
00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:45.600
What's up with Angela's outfit?

615
00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:46.780
What is it?

616
00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:50.380
It is a poofy, floofy sweater.

617
00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:51.320
Oh, yeah.

618
00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:54.260
But it's like poofy, like at the shoulder.

619
00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:57.400
That was really in, and I feel like that's coming back.

620
00:22:57.600 --> 00:22:57.920
What?

621
00:22:58.140 --> 00:22:59.340
Like the poofy arMs.

622
00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:00.020
Oh.

623
00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:04.620
We went through a real Shakespeare Renaissance fair thing back then.

624
00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:05.880
I'm not here for it.

625
00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:07.540
It's coming back, lady.

626
00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:08.180
Great.

627
00:23:08.480 --> 00:23:09.980
You know what I found in my closet?

628
00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:11.820
How do I describe this?

629
00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:15.340
I found a ribbon on a hanger.

630
00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:24.720
And then clipped to the ribbon were various flowers that I could put in my hair or on my lapel.

631
00:23:24.860 --> 00:23:26.580
You could adorn your outfit.

632
00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:32.020
Like one of the flowers was like a fabric flower that you would clip on your blazer.

633
00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:32.840
Oh, yeah.

634
00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:34.720
Was that in for a while?

635
00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:39.080
Why do I have seven flowers to clip to myself?

636
00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:40.020
I don't know.

637
00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:46.960
Oh, it feels very much like a pretty and pink, kind of like a Molly Ringwald with a flower on her hat.

638
00:23:47.180 --> 00:23:50.620
Yeah, it brought back no memories when I looked at it.

639
00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:53.180
Two of the flowers were like Hawaiian flowers.

640
00:23:53.180 --> 00:23:56.980
I clearly bought them to clip in my hair while on a trip to Hawaii.

641
00:23:57.360 --> 00:24:01.760
But the rest were more casual, more everyday.

642
00:24:01.760 --> 00:24:07.440
But I'm going to clip one on my blazer lapel when we do our book tour.

643
00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:08.640
All right?

644
00:24:08.740 --> 00:24:10.240
I'm planting that seed now.

645
00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:11.200
I can't wait.

646
00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:12.640
It's going to make me real happy.

647
00:24:12.840 --> 00:24:19.160
What I won't have on our book tour is a poofy sleeve sweater because at my age, I don't need any extra poofs.

648
00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:19.900
You know what?

649
00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:22.100
I'm going to say you will wear that on our book tour.

650
00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:23.960
No, don't say that.

651
00:24:24.120 --> 00:24:27.760
Poofy sweater thing and flower lapel.

652
00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:29.460
Who are we on this book tour?

653
00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:30.460
I don't know.

654
00:24:30.640 --> 00:24:31.900
We're interesting people.

655
00:24:32.180 --> 00:24:33.940
Well, we'll see.

656
00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:36.240
Not dressed well, but interesting.

657
00:24:36.900 --> 00:24:37.820
All right.

658
00:24:38.040 --> 00:24:39.380
Let's get started.

659
00:24:39.860 --> 00:24:44.860
This episode opens with Michael exiting a motel room.

660
00:24:45.340 --> 00:24:48.400
He knocks on the neighboring door and out comes Pam.

661
00:24:49.040 --> 00:24:49.320
Yes.

662
00:24:49.460 --> 00:24:52.880
And in the shooting draft of our script, it says Michael knocks on Pam's door.

663
00:24:53.400 --> 00:24:54.760
They say good morning.

664
00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:55.920
That's it.

665
00:24:56.140 --> 00:24:58.400
They don't even have dialogue written out for you guys.

666
00:24:58.560 --> 00:24:59.860
You just sort of greet each other.

667
00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:01.760
This is not in the script.

668
00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:03.840
When Michael knocks, says hello, good morning.

669
00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:04.820
Pam says good morning.

670
00:25:05.040 --> 00:25:06.180
And then Michael says, you ready?

671
00:25:06.420 --> 00:25:08.540
And we're off like a herd of turtles.

672
00:25:09.020 --> 00:25:10.600
That is not in the script.

673
00:25:11.560 --> 00:25:13.320
I think Steve improvised that.

674
00:25:13.320 --> 00:25:18.740
I will tell you, I absolutely loved doing this episode because I got Steve all to myself.

675
00:25:18.920 --> 00:25:19.420
I bet.

676
00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:22.200
Just scene after scene of me and Steve.

677
00:25:22.420 --> 00:25:23.280
And I loved it.

678
00:25:23.580 --> 00:25:28.700
Some of my favorite times in the office were when I just got to have days with Steve, me and Steve.

679
00:25:29.080 --> 00:25:29.620
I know.

680
00:25:29.820 --> 00:25:33.540
They were brief and few and far between because, you know, Angela Martin hated him.

681
00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.700
But those were always such a delight.

682
00:25:36.140 --> 00:25:40.260
Well, I love this scene of me putting the luggage into the back of the car.

683
00:25:40.860 --> 00:25:41.700
I did too.

684
00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:42.300
I'm sorry.

685
00:25:42.460 --> 00:25:43.160
I thought I did.

686
00:25:43.160 --> 00:25:44.540
I'm going to toot my own horn.

687
00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:47.600
I thought my heavy luggage acting was superb.

688
00:25:47.840 --> 00:25:50.360
It was so great that I wrote a question for you.

689
00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:51.840
Here's my fan question.

690
00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:52.260
Okay.

691
00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:53.360
What was in the bag?

692
00:25:53.360 --> 00:25:54.400
It looked really heavy.

693
00:25:54.680 --> 00:25:56.360
There was almost nothing in that bag.

694
00:25:56.520 --> 00:25:57.960
That was all me.

695
00:25:59.440 --> 00:26:00.160
Thank you.

696
00:26:00.760 --> 00:26:02.900
I mean, I couldn't be prouder of that.

697
00:26:03.100 --> 00:26:03.580
You know what?

698
00:26:03.640 --> 00:26:06.580
I won a Cone Award for my precision driving.

699
00:26:06.920 --> 00:26:09.220
I'm going to get you a little tiny suitcase.

700
00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:09.920
Thank you.

701
00:26:09.920 --> 00:26:12.120
That says great prop work.

702
00:26:12.280 --> 00:26:13.660
Prop work award.

703
00:26:14.080 --> 00:26:18.480
I don't know if you noticed, but we got a lot of mail about this car.

704
00:26:19.180 --> 00:26:23.420
Adele M wrote in and said, whose maroon Ford is Pam driving?

705
00:26:23.700 --> 00:26:27.740
I thought she had a Yaris and Michael had a PT Cruiser.

706
00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:28.680
What is this car?

707
00:26:28.880 --> 00:26:29.400
Exactly.

708
00:26:29.780 --> 00:26:30.900
Is it a rental car?

709
00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:32.780
Listen to this.

710
00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:33.100
What?

711
00:26:33.100 --> 00:26:35.340
This is a gem from Randy Cordray.

712
00:26:35.860 --> 00:26:41.740
He said in an early concept meeting for this episode, it was discussed that Michael would

713
00:26:41.740 --> 00:26:47.680
need extra trunk space for all of his props and his trunk and all that stuff, and that

714
00:26:47.680 --> 00:26:49.640
it just wouldn't fit in his PT Cruiser.

715
00:26:49.640 --> 00:26:55.820
So they said that they thought it would be funny if Michael had to ask the company to provide him

716
00:26:55.820 --> 00:27:00.520
with a Lincoln Town car that Pam would drive him around in.

717
00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:05.300
But corporate would only approve a cheaper Crown Victoria.

718
00:27:06.160 --> 00:27:12.020
So this was always intended to be like a scripted moment where we would explain this, but in

719
00:27:12.020 --> 00:27:13.900
the end, it never made the shooting draft.

720
00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:17.520
So it comes off a bit confusing, but this was like a whole joke.

721
00:27:17.700 --> 00:27:20.860
I love it because Michael thinks he's Carrot Top, right?

722
00:27:20.860 --> 00:27:26.800
So he's got to have all of his props and his trunks of crazy gadgets and things.

723
00:27:26.980 --> 00:27:29.040
I mean, I'm surprised he didn't dress in a costume.

724
00:27:29.580 --> 00:27:30.660
I was too.

725
00:27:30.660 --> 00:27:37.620
But yet he gives Pam like some sass about her outfit and says, don't you know what a magician's

726
00:27:37.620 --> 00:27:38.960
assistant looks like?

727
00:27:39.340 --> 00:27:41.880
I Googled magician's assistant costume.

728
00:27:42.860 --> 00:27:44.120
There's a lot of fishnet.

729
00:27:44.480 --> 00:27:45.700
There's some short shorts.

730
00:27:45.940 --> 00:27:47.060
There's a bustier.

731
00:27:47.400 --> 00:27:48.440
There's a top hat.

732
00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:48.880
Yeah.

733
00:27:49.100 --> 00:27:49.860
Sometimes a skirt.

734
00:27:49.860 --> 00:27:51.780
It's a very sexy looking outfit.

735
00:27:52.100 --> 00:27:52.380
Yeah.

736
00:27:52.620 --> 00:27:55.840
Well, Pam wore her tan cardigan.

737
00:27:56.040 --> 00:27:56.780
It's new.

738
00:27:59.520 --> 00:28:04.760
I had such a hard time getting through that line because, of course, we knew that line

739
00:28:04.760 --> 00:28:05.680
was going to be in the script.

740
00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:10.780
So when we picked my outfit for this episode, we thought it was very funny that her new cardigan

741
00:28:10.780 --> 00:28:11.780
was like...

742
00:28:11.780 --> 00:28:12.380
Beige.

743
00:28:12.480 --> 00:28:13.000
Was beige.

744
00:28:15.120 --> 00:28:19.500
I have another amazing tidbit about this car before we get on the road.

745
00:28:19.860 --> 00:28:20.720
The toboggan?

746
00:28:20.940 --> 00:28:21.240
Yeah.

747
00:28:21.480 --> 00:28:22.460
That's on top of the car?

748
00:28:22.820 --> 00:28:23.340
All right.

749
00:28:23.620 --> 00:28:29.620
The reason that's there is because there was a scene that was written as a tag for this

750
00:28:29.620 --> 00:28:30.060
episode.

751
00:28:30.340 --> 00:28:36.440
And the scene was going to be Michael and Pam going down a snowy hill on that toboggan.

752
00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:38.300
Why didn't that happen?

753
00:28:40.990 --> 00:28:41.550
Yes.

754
00:28:42.010 --> 00:28:44.150
Well, we'd have to go somewhere with snow.

755
00:28:45.490 --> 00:28:49.230
Randy said they went out to scout a snowy mountain.

756
00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:53.870
And the photos that they came back with, it just didn't look great.

757
00:28:54.070 --> 00:28:58.170
There just wasn't a lot of snow happening at the time that we were shooting this episode.

758
00:28:58.210 --> 00:29:02.430
We couldn't go all the way to Mammoth, which is five hours away, right?

759
00:29:02.430 --> 00:29:05.870
We had to find some place that was relatively close.

760
00:29:05.950 --> 00:29:07.810
And there just was no snow.

761
00:29:07.990 --> 00:29:09.470
So we never shot it.

762
00:29:09.590 --> 00:29:10.870
But there were two options.

763
00:29:11.170 --> 00:29:17.450
One was that Michael was going to be going down the hill on the toboggan and Pam was

764
00:29:17.450 --> 00:29:19.210
just going to be kind of like standing there.

765
00:29:19.650 --> 00:29:20.170
Right.

766
00:29:20.170 --> 00:29:26.610
And the other version is that Pam and Michael are sledding down together, but midway down

767
00:29:26.610 --> 00:29:29.670
the hill, Pam falls off and rolls to the bottom.

768
00:29:29.670 --> 00:29:31.130
And Michael says, again!

769
00:29:32.850 --> 00:29:36.070
Well, maybe I'm glad you didn't have to do that, Jenna Fisher.

770
00:29:36.350 --> 00:29:39.370
No, I so wish I could have gone sledding with Steve.

771
00:29:39.370 --> 00:29:40.690
I so wish.

772
00:29:40.790 --> 00:29:41.890
That would have been a blaSt.

773
00:29:42.490 --> 00:29:47.310
Back at Dunder Mifflin, Kelly arrives to work and she is really upset.

774
00:29:47.510 --> 00:29:47.670
Yeah.

775
00:29:47.670 --> 00:29:52.170
I would like to note at four minutes, 10 seconds, there is a big door slam.

776
00:29:52.630 --> 00:29:54.350
Guys, that front door did not slam.

777
00:29:54.590 --> 00:29:54.970
No.

778
00:29:55.210 --> 00:29:55.810
It did not.

779
00:29:55.930 --> 00:30:00.210
In fact, it had that little suspension thing, you know, that suspension bracket.

780
00:30:00.210 --> 00:30:05.570
So it just would shut like, so that was added in poSt.

781
00:30:05.890 --> 00:30:12.630
They had to make it a silent door because a lot of times people would have to enter and

782
00:30:12.630 --> 00:30:15.310
we'd be in the middle of a scene and then you would have heard ka-chunk.

783
00:30:15.530 --> 00:30:15.770
Right.

784
00:30:15.770 --> 00:30:20.030
So it was a, does not slam.

785
00:30:20.270 --> 00:30:20.510
Right.

786
00:30:20.670 --> 00:30:23.870
But they needed to really sell how mad Kelly was.

787
00:30:24.010 --> 00:30:25.130
So they put it in.

788
00:30:25.230 --> 00:30:25.810
Fakie slam.

789
00:30:26.530 --> 00:30:30.570
Well, Mindy says, screw you, to Jim and Dwight.

790
00:30:31.190 --> 00:30:37.010
She storms off and then Phyllis explains that Kelly is upset because they forgot her birthday

791
00:30:37.010 --> 00:30:37.570
yesterday.

792
00:30:38.110 --> 00:30:38.330
Yeah.

793
00:30:39.070 --> 00:30:40.770
We got a piece of mail.

794
00:30:40.950 --> 00:30:41.250
Okay.

795
00:30:41.470 --> 00:30:42.450
From Zoe S.

796
00:30:42.610 --> 00:30:43.890
Here's what Zoe has to say.

797
00:30:44.710 --> 00:30:47.530
In this episode, it's the day after Kelly's birthday.

798
00:30:48.010 --> 00:30:48.990
Jim and Dwight forgot.

799
00:30:49.790 --> 00:30:52.670
Phyllis knew it was Kelly's birthday yesterday.

800
00:30:53.190 --> 00:30:56.590
But Kelly says nobody wished her a happy birthday.

801
00:30:57.470 --> 00:31:03.310
Zoe would like to know, why didn't Phyllis wish Kelly a happy birthday if she knew?

802
00:31:03.310 --> 00:31:08.230
I mean, it's one thing that Phyllis wants to make Jim and Dwight look bad, but Phyllis

